cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "aphylo" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'aphylo: Statistical Inference and Prediction of Annotations in Phylogenetic
  Trees'
version: 0.3-6
doi: 10.32614/CRAN.package.aphylo
abstract: Implements a parsimonious evolutionary model to analyze and predict gene-functional
  annotations in phylogenetic trees as described in Vega Yon et al. (2021) <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007948>.
  Focusing on computational efficiency, 'aphylo' makes it possible to estimate pooled
  phylogenetic models, including thousands (hundreds) of annotations (trees) in the
  same run. The package also provides the tools for visualization of annotated phylogenies,
  calculation of posterior probabilities (prediction) and goodness-of-fit assessment
  featured in Vega Yon et al. (2021).
